[252.479, "add\u001b[26Gonly\u001b[31Gabout\u001b[37G1\u001b[39Gms\u001b[42Gover\u001b[47G289\u001b[51Gforwards,\u001b[61Gso\u001b[64Gthe\u001b[68Gmatmuls\u001b[76Gmust\u001b[81Gexplain\u001b[89Gthe\u001b[93Gdrift,\u001b[100Gwhich\u001b[106Gis\u001b[109Gprobably\r\u001b[1B  system noise. I'm now running the earlier build (/tmp/c1v3/A) interleaved with the current one to confirm.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[39m The current build matches or slightly beats the earlier one in interleaved runs, so the earlier drift was machine\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B noise. I'm running the\u001b[26Gfull regression suite on the final code next.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m \u001b[39m Full regression\u001b[19Gsuite on final code\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m  \u23bf  $ ./build.sh && python3 check.py -- ./run_c1 | tail -1 && python3 check.py --tokens 64 --prompts 3 -- ./run_c1 | \r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[4G  \u001b[38;2;102;102;102mgrep -E \"error|PASS|FAIL\" | sort -k5 -g | tail -2 && python3 -I tests/difftest.py \"$PWD\" && python3 -I \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;102;102;102mtests/longctx.py \""]
